<title>USA: Union Pacific well flows 84.7 mmcfd.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific well flows 84.7 mmcfd.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Resources Group Inc said on Tuesday that its Eberle No.1 well flowed at 84.7 million cubic feet of natural gas in a 24 hour period from the Austin Chalk formation in Washington County, Texas.</p>
<p>The company said the well is the largest horizontal gas well ever drilled onshore in the United States, based on initial flow rates.  </p>
<p>.</p>
</text>
